  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 303 AM EST Sun Nov 8 2026\n\nPleasant and dry weather continues through the middle of the \nupcoming week with high pressure over the region. Temperatures will \nwarm up slightly, but remain around normal with highs in the 70s, \nand overnight lows in the upper 30s to low 40s. Confidence in the \ndetails of the forecast start to drop off in the Thursday-Friday \ntimeframe, but the general consensus is that a strong trough amd \nassociated cold front will move across the Eastern US and bring at \nleast slight rain chances to our area. It is looking increasingly \nlikely that the coolest airmass of the season thus far would move in \nfor next weekend, with lows approaching or even falling below \nfreezing across much of the area. High temperatures during this \ntimeframe would likely top out in the 50s to low 60s.",
